# Throwaway refactor scripts written into the repo root during a session.
# The real, kept tooling lives in tools/ and is committed deliberately; anything
# else at the root matching this is scratch that `git add -A` would otherwise
# sweep in -- three of them reached commits before this rule existed.
/*.py
.kotlin

# The Play upload key and the Play service-account key are credentials: they live in CI secrets,
# never in the repo. The checked-in app/debug.keystore is deliberately tracked (every CI build is
# signed with the same key, so builds install over each other) and is unaffected by these patterns.
*.keystore
*.jks
play-service-account.json

